gpui: Preserve native keyboard metadata for terminal input

Key events carry the physical key and the original layout and modifier
metadata, without changing shortcut matching. macOS and Windows supply
layout metadata; Linux and web keep optional fallbacks. Window::numlock()
reads the current lock state, implemented on Windows. Synthetic events carry
no native metadata.

Newport needs it for terminal key encoding. KeyDownEvent and KeyUpEvent gain
optional fields, so struct literals downstream must set them.

Remove when GPUI exposes physical keys and layout metadata on key events.

